-- title:
--   Lemma 11 — shrinking dartboard: $\tilde I_t\sim\pi_t$, regret and switch bounds
-- statement:
--   Let $\eta>0$ and let $g_1,\dots,g_T\in[0,\infty)^K$ be random loss vectors with $\mathbb Eg_t(i)<\infty$, such that each $g_t$ is independent of the arm $\tilde I_t$ given $g_1,\dots,g_{t-1}$. Let $\pi_t$ be exponential weights with learning rate $\eta$ from the uniform distribution, $\pi_{t+1,i}\propto\pi_{t,i}e^{-\eta g_t(i)}$, and $\tilde I_1\sim\pi_1$. After round $t<T$, the arm is kept if a keeping coin succeeds and is otherwise replaced by a resampling draw; conditional on $(g_1,\dots,g_t,\tilde I_t)$ the coin and the draw are independent with laws $\mathrm{Bernoulli}(e^{-\eta g_t(\tilde I_t)})$ and $\pi_{t+1}$. Then, given $g_1,\dots,g_t$, the arm $\tilde I_t$ has law $\pi_t$, and for every $i\in[K]$
--   $$
--   \mathbb E\sum_{t=1}^Tg_t(\tilde I_t)-\mathbb E\sum_{t=1}^Tg_t(i)\le\frac{\log K}{\eta}+\frac\eta2\,\mathbb E\sum_{t=1}^T\langle\pi_t,g_t^2\rangle,\qquad
--   \mathbb E\sum_{t=2}^T\mathbf 1\{\tilde I_t\ne\tilde I_{t-1}\}\le\eta\,\mathbb E\sum_{t=1}^T\langle\pi_t,g_t\rangle .
--   $$
--   The arm follows exponential weights in law while switching rarely.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Rounds are 0-based. Conditioning is on the σ-algebras generated by $(g_0,\dots,g_{t-1})$ and by $((g_0,\dots,g_t),\tilde I_t)$; conditional independence and laws are stated through conditional expectations of indicators. All random elements are measurable.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: conditional independence and conditional laws of g_t, Ĩ_t, the keeping coin and the resampling draw → product rules and values for conditional expectations of indicators given the generated σ-algebras; Ĩ_1 uniform; all random elements measurable; reason: for discrete variables these are the definitions of conditional independence and conditional law; measurability is implicit in "random"; same instances
--   - encoding: the regret bound with right-hand side E Σ⟨π_t, g_t²⟩ → the bound under the hypothesis that ⟨π_t, g_t²⟩ is integrable for every t; reason: otherwise the paper's right-hand side is +∞ and the bound holds trivially; the hypothesis excludes only that case and Lean's junk integral 0
-- source:
--   Cesa-Bianchi, Cesari, Colomboni, Esposito, Fusco, Koren, The Price of Partial Information with Switching Costs, arXiv:2606.03851 (held version, sha256 ded8f8bc…), Lemma 11, p.33 (PDF p.35); the method, p.33

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_UnderstandingML_Online
open MeasureTheory

namespace FeedbackSwitching

/-- **Lemma 11 (Shrinking dartboard)**, p.33 (PDF p.35). Cesa-Bianchi, Cesari, Colomboni, Esposito, Fusco, Koren, *The Price of Partial Information with
Switching Costs: A Complete Characterization for Feedback Graphs*, arXiv:2606.03851 (held version,
sha256 ded8f8bc…).

Let `η > 0`, and let `g_1, …, g_T ∈ [0, ∞)^K` be random loss vectors such that each `g_t` is
independent of `Ĩ_t` given `g_1, …, g_{t−1}`. For each `t < T`, conditional on `(g_1, …, g_t, Ĩ_t)`,
the keeping coin and the resampling draw are independent, with respective distributions
`Bernoulli(e^{−ηg_t(Ĩ_t)})` and `π_{t+1}`. Assume additionally that `E g_t(i) < ∞` for every
`t ∈ [T]` and `i ∈ [K]`. Then, given `g_1, …, g_t`, the arm `Ĩ_t` has law `π_t`. Moreover, for
every `i ∈ [K]`,
`E ∑_{t=1}^T g_t(Ĩ_t) − E ∑_{t=1}^T g_t(i) ≤ log K/η + (η/2) E ∑_{t=1}^T ⟨π_t, g_t²⟩` and
`E ∑_{t=2}^T 1{Ĩ_t ≠ Ĩ_{t−1}} ≤ η E ∑_{t=1}^T ⟨π_t, g_t⟩`.

The method (§6.1, p.33): `π_t` is exponential weights with learning rate `η` from the uniform
distribution, `π_{t+1,i} ∝ π_{t,i} e^{−ηg_t(i)}`; `Ĩ_1 ∼ π_1`; after round `t` the arm is kept if the
keeping coin succeeds and is otherwise the resampling draw.

**Formalization Note.** Rounds are 0-based (`t < T`). `π_t = wmWeights η g t`. Conditioning on
`g_1, …, g_{t−1}` is the conditional expectation given the σ-algebra generated by
`(g_0, …, g_{t−1})`, and on `(g_1, …, g_t, Ĩ_t)` given the σ-algebra generated by
`((g_0, …, g_t), Ĩ_t)`. Conditional independence of `g_t` and `Ĩ_t` is the product rule for the
indicators of `{g_t ∈ S}` and `{Ĩ_t = j}`; the joint conditional law of the Boolean keeping coin and
the draw `J_t` is the product of the two stated laws. All random elements are measurable. The
regret bound is stated when its right-hand side is finite (`⟨π_t, g_t²⟩` integrable); otherwise
the paper's right-hand side is `+∞` and the bound holds trivially. -/
theorem lemma_11 {Ω : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    {K : ℕ} [NeZero K] (T : ℕ) (η : ℝ) (hη : 0 < η)
    (g : ℕ → Ω → Fin K → ℝ) (hg_meas : ∀ t, Measurable (g t))
    (hg_nonneg : ∀ t ω i, 0 ≤ g t ω i)
    (hg_int : ∀ t < T, ∀ i, Integrable (fun ω => g t ω i) μ)
    (I : ℕ → Ω → Fin K) (hI_meas : ∀ t, Measurable (I t))
    (keep : ℕ → Ω → Bool) (hkeep_meas : ∀ t, Measurable (keep t))
    (J : ℕ → Ω → Fin K) (hJ_meas : ∀ t, Measurable (J t))
    (hI0 : ∀ j, μ {ω | I 0 ω = j} = ((K : ENNReal))⁻¹)
    (hindep : ∀ t < T, ∀ S : Set (Fin K → ℝ), MeasurableSet S → ∀ j,
      μ[({ω | g t ω ∈ S} ∩ {ω | I t ω = j}).indicator (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) |
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (s : Fin t) => g s ω) inferInstance]
        =ᵐ[μ]
      μ[{ω | g t ω ∈ S}.indicator (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) |
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (s : Fin t) => g s ω) inferInstance] *
      μ[{ω | I t ω = j}.indicator (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) |
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (s : Fin t) => g s ω) inferInstance])
    (hcoins : ∀ t, t + 1 < T → ∀ j,
      (μ[{ω | keep t ω = true ∧ J t ω = j}.indicator (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) |
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => ((fun s : Fin (t + 1) => g s ω), I t ω)) inferInstance]
        =ᵐ[μ] fun ω => Real.exp (-η * g t ω (I t ω)) *
          UnderstandingML.wmWeights η (fun s => g s ω) (t + 1) j) ∧
      (μ[{ω | keep t ω = false ∧ J t ω = j}.indicator (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) |
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => ((fun s : Fin (t + 1) => g s ω), I t ω)) inferInstance]
        =ᵐ[μ] fun ω => (1 - Real.exp (-η * g t ω (I t ω))) *
          UnderstandingML.wmWeights η (fun s => g s ω) (t + 1) j))
    (hstep : ∀ t ω, I (t + 1) ω = if keep t ω then I t ω else J t ω) :
    (∀ t < T, ∀ j,
      μ[{ω | I t ω = j}.indicator (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) |
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (s : Fin (t + 1)) => g s ω) inferInstance]
        =ᵐ[μ] fun ω => UnderstandingML.wmWeights η (fun s => g s ω) t j) ∧
    ((∀ t < T, Integrable (fun ω => ∑ i, UnderstandingML.wmWeights η (fun s => g s ω) t i *
        g t ω i ^ 2) μ) →
      ∀ i, (∫ ω, ∑ t ∈ Finset.range T, g t ω (I t ω) ∂μ) - ∫ ω, ∑ t ∈ Finset.range T, g t ω i ∂μ
        ≤ Real.log K / η + η / 2 * ∫ ω, ∑ t ∈ Finset.range T,
            ∑ i, UnderstandingML.wmWeights η (fun s => g s ω) t i * g t ω i ^ 2 ∂μ) ∧
    ∫ ω, ∑ t ∈ Finset.range (T - 1), (if I (t + 1) ω ≠ I t ω then (1 : ℝ) else 0) ∂μ
      ≤ η * ∫ ω, ∑ t ∈ Finset.range T,
          ∑ i, UnderstandingML.wmWeights η (fun s => g s ω) t i * g t ω i ∂μ := by sorry

end FeedbackSwitching
